      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common high-risk indicators to recognize during stops include strong verbal or body language aggression, such as raised voices, clenched fists, or squinting eyes; rapid movements or gestures towards the officer or vehicle; and verbal warnings or threats, such as \"I'll handle this\" or \"Don't touch me.\" Additionally, look for signs of resistance or non-compliance, like attempted escapes or deliberate failing to comply with instructions. officers should also be aware of cultural and linguistic communication differences that may lead to misInterpretation or misunderstandings. \n\n Officers should also be attentive to environmental factors, such as loud noises, pouring rain, or high levels of foot traffic, which can amplify tension or create additional stress.",
